# Harness discipline

Enforced in agent workflow, not only CI. See `.cursor/rules/harness-artifacts.mdc` for paths.

## Tracks

- **Feature** (new feature / big adjustment): GitHub issue + plan → generate → review. Keep the issue updated.
- **Direct** (feedback / finetune / bugs): no harness folders required; implement on `development`.

## Always (Feature track)

- **GitHub issue** (or create one) for every **feature** — discussion on GitHub; AC in local `docs/project/issues/<n>/`.
- **plan → generate** - lighten artefacts for S/micro-S; **review is often skipped** (see reviewer-defaults); never overbuild the plan or reviewer set.
- Update **`docs/project/generator-state.md`** when Feature implementation state changes.
- Update **`docs/project/roadmap.md`** when a Feature issue closes.
- **`CHANGELOG.md`** - every cycle close: specific bullets + patch **+0.0.1** + finish date ([changelog](changelog.mdc)); required for S / user-facing work.
- Designs = **HTML** only when [design-when](design-when.mdc) applies (components or L/XL) - no mockup images; visual UI only; **no** approval pause. S-M skip designer by default.
- Verify with **relevant** `setup.md` commands for touched surfaces - not every gate on every change.

## Feedback layout (Feature track)

One folder per issue: `docs/project/feedback/<n>/` where `<n>` is the GitHub issue number.

Filenames: `<reviewer-type>-i<iteration>.md`, `generator-response-i<iteration>.md`

Reviewers **own** their files; generator **only** writes `generator-response-i*.md`.

Prior iteration files are **immutable** - add new files for the next round.

## Generator must not author

- `code-review-i*.md`, `api-review-i*.md`, `security-review-i*.md`, `frontend-eval-i*.md`, `mcp-review-i*.md`, `database-review-i*.md`, `performance-eval-i*.md`, `docs-review-i*.md`

## Reviewers must not

- Implement fixes in the same pass as review
- Edit generator-owned `generator-response-i*.md`
- Mutate a previous iteration's review file

## ADRs

- **accepted** ADRs are binding; **proposed** are not.
- Generator stops if implementation needs a fork not covered by an accepted ADR → invoke `architect`, wait for human acceptance.
- Architectural changes need linked ADR (`code-reviewer` flags gaps).

## Lifecycle

Check `docs/project/project.md` → **Lifecycle stage** (MVP / Live / Mature) before large refactors. See `.cursor/rules/lifecycle-change.mdc`.

## Exceptions

`skip-harness-check` note + reason - rare, human-approved only (Feature track).
